                Preface

In the journey of success, the adventures and experiences along the
path are as vital, if not more vital, than arrival at the destination. Thus,
in the quest for success, the attributes and attitudes one develops and
what one becomes due to the demands of the journey are more
profound, lasting and beneficial than the things one acquires for getting
to the destination.

Like all journeys to the unknown, the value of a tour guide in the
journey of success is untold. Wisdom is a principal guide in the journey
of life. At every point, it tells what to do, which way to go, where to
take a bend, when to halt, whom to walk with and many other crucial
decisions in the course of the journey. Wisdom prevents from errors
thereby increasing one’s chances of safe arrival to destiny.

The Wisdom of God is the foundation upon which the entire universe
runs. Access to Divine Wisdom is like having the architect who
designed the plans of a very complex mansion showing one around the
building. One can not miss the way when the person who designed the
blueprint is the one showing the way.

                                                              vi
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

This book focuses on Wisdom, especially as it relates to making a
success out of your life, vision and destiny. The principles are simple
and profound. They are based on the God’s word. The principles
communicated in this book will serve different purposes to different
categories of people. Some principles communicated are things you
already are aware of, this book will serve to strengthen your conviction.
Some are things you need to see from another perspective, they will
correct your opinions. Some are things you are already practicing,
thereby explaining your results.
Whichever way this book comes across to you, you will be encouraged,
challenged, inspired and enlightened.

                                                             Vii
                                 CHAPTER 1

             THE WISDOM OF IDEAS

When one prays for a harvest, God gives a seed. What one does with
the seed determines whether the harvest will ever be received or not.
Merely understanding this simple but profound truth makes one
understand that God has answered many of the prayers people prayed
but they did not recognize the answers when they came. This justifies
God from human predicaments and places the onus of man’s limiting
experiences on him. God gives every one a seed but the responsibility
of what each one does with his/her seeds lies them. Do you despise
your seeds? Do you neglect, discard, destroy, bury, eat or expose them
to predators? Do you plant and nurture your seeds?

Ideas are major seeds for success. Ideas are like embryos, conceived in
the womb of the mind, which when fully gestated, are delivered as
Success in real-life. Conceiving, developing and executing ideas is one
major distinguishing factor between successful people and failures.
Imagine how successful and high impact your life would have been
right now if you had successfully executed all the wonderful ideas that
ever flickered through your mind. Are you not guilty of non-execution
of having aborted a thousand unborn ‘Success-Children’?

In Matthew 13:31, Jesus told a parable, "The Kingdom of Heaven is like
a mustard seed planted in a field. It is the smallest all seeds, but it becomes
the largest of garden plants; it grows into a tree, and birds come and make
nests in its branches." (NLT).

                                                               1
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

Seeds become trees and then birds find home and nest on the tree.
Ideas are intangible seeds but when ‘planted’, they become mighty
trees. The full potential of the idea in your mind is that many other
people will begin to find solace in the tangible structure that the idea
will produce. Your idea may be the next ‘tree’ where numerous
unemployed people will find a ‘nest’. Your idea has the capability to
accommodate and bless multitudes when you ‘plant’ it. It is a kingdom
principle that if you can execute your idea, however small it may be, it
will gradually grow so big that other people can be accommodated in
it.

Prov. 10:22 says, “The blessing of the Lord makes one rich...” (NKJV).
God’s blessing is the source of riches, wealth and success. This shows
that the blessing is not money and riches but has the ability to produce
them. Money and riches are tangible while the blessing is intangible.
The blessing of God, among many other spiritual equivalents, comes in
the form of concepts, insights, ideas, skills, graces and abilities that
God endows a man with to employ for success. Insights, concepts and
ideas are blessings from the spiritual realm.

A lot of people have been taught to give offerings and tithes so as to
reap financial harvests. However, many have not been well-taught to
recognize the harvest when it comes. One may give money and God
doesn’t necessarily reward them with a harvest of cash but with an idea
and ability. It is the person’s job to convert those endowments into
money. Therefore, when God wants to make a person successful, He
gives him an idea, insight, concept, vision or an instruction - all these
come as intangible ideas.

The power of one Idea

The successful people of today are those who relentlessly pursued their
ideas of yesterday. The successful people of tomorrow are those who
are executing their ideas of today.

                                                               2
                                                 WISDOM OF IDEAS

You might have wasted your ideas in past years but do not live in
regrets, decide to discipline yourselves to gainfully employ the ideas of
today. The good thing is that you do not need a multitude of ideas to
become great. One divine idea, acted upon and maximized, is sufficient
to change one’s life forever.

In human biology, millions of sperms are released at ejaculation, the
first to make it to ovum fertilizes it while the rest die. The one in a
million sperm that made it grows to become a living being who later
manufactures jet engines, designs complex computer systems, builds
skyscrapers and oversees multinational conglomerates. The greatness
of human life is not in the million that died but the one that made it.
Similarly, no matter how many ideas were conceived and aborted in the
womb of your mind, there is still sufficient space and time for success
in the one idea that you will conceive and execute now irrespective of
the past. You can still be a success as long as you have not become
barren of ideas and you make a new resolution to follow through on
your ideas.

Ideas are as Real as Cash

Idea is capital. You are really poor if you have no ideas. An idea is
potential money, greatness and success. In the mental and spiritual
realms, ideas are as concrete and tangible as brick. The Biblical
account of the Great Flood that happened thousands of years ago
showed that God destroyed the earth, not only because of human evil
actions but the evil ideas. People’s ideas are as important as their
actions in determining the direction of their destinies. In Gen 6:5 we
see that God decided to destroy the earth with a flood because the Lord
saw that the wickedness of man was great in the earth, and that every
imagination and intention of all human thinking was only evil continually.
(AMP).

                                                               3
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

In other words, God was as concerned about the wickedness of human
actions as He was with the wickedness of their thoughts and intentions.
The evil of their actions were worrisome but God knew that a higher
threshold of evil was imminent when He examined their ideas. Thus,
one could accurately predict people’s future if one could peep into the
kinds of ideas they nurture in their minds. Choose to fill your mind
with ideas of wealth, greatness, success and increase. It is time for you
to consider, respect, protect, nurture, manage and care for your ideas
as you would do to your most prized tangible possessions.

In Gen 11:3-7, the people on the earth conceived an idea to build a
tower in defiance to God. The Bible then records, but the Lord came
down to see the city and the tower which the sons of men had built. We
know for certainty that the building had not been physically completed
as at the time of this scriptural verse because the story proceeded to tell
how God stopped them from completing the project. However, the
Bible says that ‘God came down to see the city and the tower which the
sons of men had built’. An unfinished project was referenced in the past
participle because, as far as God was concerned, the tower was as good
as built the moment the idea was conceived nurtured and acted upon!

God attacked the project at the idea stage because He knew if He
didn’t stop them, they would achieve in the physical realm the idea that
had conceived in the mental realm. God stopped them by confusing
their language so they will not be able to communicate and further
develop their idea. He did not send hail, fire or a battalion of warring
angles to fight them, He simply attacked their ability to communicate
ideas. Idea and strategy battles are more potent than the physical
physical warfare. People win or lose in the realm of ideas.

                                                               4
                                                 WISDOM OF IDEAS

Ideas Rule

Ideas are more real than cash. Ideas are more concrete than block!
Ideas are potent than weapons. The realm of the spirit respect ideas.
God understands the power of ideas and satan does too. This is the
reason satan is keen on fighting your success and prosperity by
attacking them at the idea stage.

If God gives you an idea worth a billion dollars then He reckons
Himself to have given one billion dollars. This shows your prayer to
become a billionaire was answered by God long ago, you only need to
place a higher premium on your ideas. You need to value, respect and
believe in them. Don’t take them for granted.

It is amazing that we take an inventory of our lives, we take stock of
our real estate, cars, gadgets, clothing, certificates and material
possession as our esteemed assets while forgetting to reckon our most
valuable assets - our ideas and our inherent abilities.

Ideas rule the world. Every great thing started as an idea. Therefore, in
the school of success, you must master the course of birthing your
ideas to reality. The following are what to do with ideas for them to
become tangible structures that will reward you.

Steps From Ideas to Reality

Great people are those who follow through on ideas to the reality stage.
The following are steps to take in translating ideas to reality.

     Conceive the Ideas: You must master the art of conceiving ideas.
     Solitude is an art of royalty; when it comes to conception and
     gestating ideas. Meditation and observation are instruments for
     generating ideas. Divine ideas come as revelation into spirit.

                                                               5
                                        WISDOM FOR LIVING

Write the Ideas: Writing is a royal behavior. If it is said that readers
are leaders, then what should be said of the ones that write what is
read. Writers are the leaders and influencers of leaders. Writing is a
divine attribute. God instructed many men in the Bible to write
down what they see. (Ex. 17: 14, Jer. 36: 2, Hab. 2:2, Rev. 1: 19).
Ideas are worth so little unless they are caught on paper and ink.
Very powerful ideas could be so fleeting that if not timely captured,
they will pass away with all the great benefit inherent in them. Have
an ideas room where you meditate, have an ideas book where you
write down your ideas.

Develop the Ideas: Idea development starts with the writing phase,
as writing forces one to think constructively and articulately.
However, writing is not all there is to idea development. Research,
consultation and analysis are part of developing ideas. There is
need to study cases of successful executions of related ideas, share
the ideas with positive minded individual and organize vision-
casting and brain-storming sessions, pitch your ideas to
stakeholders. Do you now see why people usually do not pursue
their ideas, developing an idea is already tedious enough a job, how
much more the strenuous work of execution.

Execute the Ideas: The test of strength of character is in execution
of ideas. No matter how great an idea is, when unexecuted, it is as
good as dead. A living dog is said to be better than a dead lion. An
executed average idea is better than an unexecuted great idea. The
proof of readiness for success is one’s ability to take steps on one’s
ideas. There is always a step one can take, no matter how small for
a start. An idea can be too daunting to attack immediately, but
there is always something little that can be done about it
immediately. It is taking the immediate small incremental steps
towards the accomplishment that opens the door for the bigger

                                                       6
          WISDOM OF IDEAS

opportunities along the line of the idea. The graveyard of ideas is doing
nothing. Avoid that pitfall by doing something strategic, no matter how
little, about your God given ideas today.

