Ideas rule the world. Cease praying for money, start praying for ideas
and the grace to execute them!

                                                               7
                                 CHAPTER 2

      THE WISDOM OF OPPORTUNITY

Ideas are the seeds for success, opportunities are the doorways to
success. A person who has developed capacity and adequately
prepared is, many times, a single opportunity away from success.
Capacity building and preparation are foundational keys to success but
ultimately it is opportunity that will eventually open the door. In every
success equation, there is a part opportunity played.

Walking with God and attain success God’s way is a partnership; there
is a part one is to play and there is a part God will play. Bringing
opportunities, many times, is God’s role. Preparation, capacity
building and acting on the opportunities are human role.

The arrival of opportunity is only beneficial to the prepared, capable
and proactive. Therefore, many prayers for success were answered
when God sent opportunities knocking at people’s door. However,
many did not recognise them, neglected them, shunned them, were not
ready for them or were too lazy and laid back for them. A great skill in
life is the ability to discern and capitalise on opportunities.
Discernment is necessary in identifying opportunities because they
come disguised many times as problems, work, questions, observation,
request or a conversation.
A classic example of the success power of opportunities is the Bible
story of Joseph, the son of Jacob, who lived in Egypt for years as a

                                                               8
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

Slave until a single moment of opportunity after years of preparation
and development of strength of character. Joseph’s day of opportunity
was the night he stood before the Pharaoh of Egypt and needed to
interpret a dream and proffer solutions to a national problem. A good
study of the story of Joseph's shows that the things he did the night he
stood before Pharaoh and landed at the peak of the government of the
Kingdom were the same things he had been doing for decades
interpreting dreams, administering systems, developing creative
solutions to problems and leading with strong character. However, he
slept as a prisoner in a cell one night and woke up on the throne the
next day as the ruler of the empire because he discerned and acted on
opportunity. He did not just interpret Pharaoh’s dreams, he proffered a
solution that made him necessary and needed. According to Gen 41:33-
40, he said, "And now let Pharaoh look for a discerning and wise man
and put him in charge of the land of Egypt . . . the plan seemed good to
Pharaoh and to all his officials. So Pharaoh asked them, "Can we find
anyone like this man, one in whom is the spirit of God?" Then Pharaoh
said to Joseph, "Since God has made all this known to you, there is no
one so discerning and wise as you. You shall be in charge of my palace,
and all my people are to submit to your orders. Only with respect to the
throne will I be greater than you."

There is untold power in a single opportunity when it meets the
prepared. When you have diligently prepared, faithfully made necessary
inputs and consistently developed yourself for years and success is still
far-fetched, then your prayer should be for God to direct the right
opportunities to you.

Opportunity Requires Promptness

Jesus said in Rev. 3: 20, "Look! I have been standing at the door, and I
am constantly knocking. If anyone hears me calling him and opens the

                                                               9
                                      THE WISDOM OF OPPORTUNITY

 door, I will come in and fellowship with him and he with me (TLB).
Contextually, this scripture is a call is to all people to open the door and
captialise on the opportunity of salvation that Jesus brings. However,
this analogy of one staying at the door knocking and waiting to be let in
applies to every form of opportunity. While Jesus waits very patiently at
the door of people’s heart for them to open to the opportunity of
salvation, other opportunities do not wait that long at the door of life.
Life changing opportunities come at a fleeting moment and it is wise to
open up to opportunities as quickly as they come knocking else they
would be as quickly gone as they came. The wisest approach to
opportunity, however, is to go out the door and seek for them and not
even wait for them to come knocking on your door.

Opportunities abound everywhere. One man’s problem is another man’s
opportunity. Fortunes hide in opportunities. While mediocrities hope
on luck, exceptional people prepare for opportunities. It is often said,
‘success is a matter of luck, ask any failure.’ The truth is that success is a
matter of opportunity engaged, ask any successful person.

The following must be done with opportunities
  1.Prepare for Opportunities: Life was designed to reward preparation
     and penalise unpreparedness. The first thing to do in positioning for
     any form of success is preparation. Preparation entails developing
     character and building capacity for success, putting systems in
     place, acquiring necessary training, skills and certifications,
     developing necessary relationships as well as saving and investing
     financially for the day of opportunity. When you think you have
     prepared and opportunity has not shown up, it means you have
     been given more opportunity to prepare for opportunity.

Prov. 21: 31 says the horse is prepared for the day of battle, but the
victory belongs to the Lord (NLT).

                                                              10
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

Preparation is not contrary to faith; in fact, the prove that you are in
faith is that you are diligently preparing. The only right use of today is
to use it to prepare for tomorrow. The quality of your life today is a
reflection of your preparations of yesterday. The quality of your
tomorrow will be a reflection of your preparation of today. A person
not preparing but waiting and hoping is wasting. While waiting for
opportunities, use the time actively to prepare, position, build capacity,
align self and put structures in place while anticipating the door of
opportunity to open.

2. Seek Opportunities: Another thing to do with opportunities is to seek
for them. Opportunity, many times, does not just come to people, it has
to be sought out. In the quest for opportunities, after adequate
preparation, another vital step is to start the search. Opportunity
searching is both a spiritual and a physical exertion. Therefore, in the
pursuit of success, preparing, scouting as well as praying for
opportunities is a necessity. Prayer, should not be limited to being a
vehicle of asking for material things, it must be rightly engaged as a
tool for receiving and developing intangible blessings - ideas and
opportunities, among many others.

There are many wrong beliefs that prevent people from accessing life
changing opportunities . Some people hold on to cliches like ‘whatever
will be will be’, ‘what is mine is mine, it will come to me where I am’’, ‘what
is mine will not go to another person but will surely come to me anyway’, ‘If
I find it difficult to get it, then it probably is not meant for me.

All these are half-truths that are disastrous to seeking opportunities.
Opportunity will not come to you anyway. An opportunity that could
have changed your life may go to another person if you do not seek it
and grab it. Opportunity is in high demand, sought out by many. It
does not have the time or patience to seek or wait for anyone.

                                                              11
                                      THE WISDOM OF OPPORTUNITY

If Opportunity doesn’t come to you and you hear that she is
somewhere, you may quickly need to go to that place to get her.

3. Create Opportunities: There are times when you seek opportunities
and you find none, so you create opportunities for yourselves. You can
create opportunities by creating a demand or need for what you can do,
creating awareness of your capacities and potentials, creating new
relationships and meeting people. In the story of Joseph before the
Pharaoh of Egypt told earlier, Joseph actually used the opportunity to
create an appointment need for himself. Quit begging people for jobs or
contracts, create opportunity for yourself by identifying a problem,
solving it even if you have to do it free foremost for them to see the
value it will bring to them.

Men are the conveyors of opportunities and sometimes creating
relationship with right people is creating opportunities. Use your
talents and gifts to create opportunities by serving them out to people.
Joseph created an opportunity for himself when he proffered a solution
and advised they employ someone to implement it. He created a niche
only He could fill.

4. Recognise Opportunities: One of the most important life skills is
recognition and discernment. A major faculty in success is the ability to
discern and recognise situations, uniqueness, opportunities, people and
times. This ability, many times, does not come naturally, it has to be
God given. The entrance of certain people into one’s life, many times,
is the coming of opportunity. However, if one does not discern and
recognise the value they represent, one misses all the possibilities they
bring. Situations and circumstances also bring inherent opportunities
which if one does not recongise, loses out on the chances and
possibilities. Truly, many look but few see. A lot of people miss
opportunity because it comes disguised.

                                                              12
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

It takes wisdom and discernment to see through and recognise the
opportunity inherent in people, places, events and situations.

5. Engage Opportunities: Finally, it is important to engage opportunities
once you spot them. Engaging opportunities needs pro-activeness and
promptness. Opportunity once came knocking at a man’s door late in
the night. The man asked who it was and opportunity replied that he
came to deliver some goods. The man, in his mind, weighed the risk
whether it was a thief or truly Opportunity that was knocking. So, he
took some time to dig the floor of his bedroom to hide all his money
and precious items and cover the floor back. He further went to get a
club and machete and keep them by the door-side. He then went to
turn on the burglary alarm and peeped through the hole of his window
to check who it was. Can you guess who he saw? Nobody! Nobody was
there. Opportunity had gone! He never had the chance to know who
had visited. However, the next day, he learned that his neighbour had
hit some stroke of fortune and would be relocating to a choicer
property in an upper part of the city. When he asked how his neighbour
could afford such expensive property, he told him about a visitor that
came to him last night and brought a huge fortune.

