hard the person prays. If Jesus obeyed the principle, then everyone
must. Discover what you have and deploy it diligently and productively
to command what you want.

Actually in life, for everyone, there is always what you have and what

you do not have. You must learn to use what you have to receive what

you do not have. Your success and prosperity is in what you have and

not in what you do not have.  18
                                      THE WISDOM OF PRODUCTIVITY

It is better to focus on what you have and not what you do not have.
Failures always focus and talk about the things they do not have to the
detriment of what they have.

Intrinsic and Extrinsic Value

While people are seeking externally for someone or something to make
them successful, genuine and lasting success only flows from inside out.
In the quest for success, success is elusive when people seek it only
externally. All profitable search for success begins internally. What will
make you successful is inherent to you and is waiting to be discovered
and unleashed.

Value can be intrinsic or extrinsic. Intrinsic value describes elements
inherent in one’s personal essence. Intrinsic value is most intangible
and consists of knowledge, skills, abilities, charisma and other things
that become the natural essence of the person once acquired. Extrinsic
values are valuable and transactable assets that are external to one’s
person. For clarity, a teacher has the classroom property and
accessories as external value while the teaching skills and knowledge of
the subject are intrinsic value.

It is great wisdom to invest first into intrinsic value before extrinsic. To

have sustainable success, it is also advisable to invest more into

intrinsic value than extrinsic. Even though, extrinsic possessions are

usually more glamorous and celebrated, people who understand the

power of delayed gratification develop intrinsic value first. The truly

successful are not in a hurry to look good, rather they are willing to

build lasting success by first taking ample time to develop intrinsic

capacity.  19
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

It is noteworthy that intrinsic values cannot be lost due to the risk
factors that affect many extrinsic possessions. An investment in
intrinsic value usually pay more dividends in the long run. Warren
Buffet, a great contemporary financial investors and one of the world’s
wealthiest men was asked what the best investment to put one’s money
in. He simply replied, ‘Yourself - The best investment is to invest in
yourself’. Extrinsic values must definitely and eventually be acquired as
one builds systems and structures around his enterprise. However,
make sure that you have built intrinsic value as a foundation to
spending resources to acquire extrinsic values. If one who has not
developed intrinsic value, loses the external assets he has acquired, he
will realize that there was no real value possessed. Certificates are
extrinsic values but skill is intrinsic value. Possessions and property are
extrinsic but knowledge and knowledge is intrinsic.

The Law of Productivity

Productivity is the art of converting valuable resources into tangible,
measurable and transactable output. Simply put, productivity is
converting one’s value to goods and services that are offered in
exchange for reward. Value talks about what you have, productivity
talks about what you do with what you have. Productivity, therefore,
involves the dispensation of value and the creation of return channels
of reward. One may be valuable but not productive; if one does not
create a structure for dispensation, perpetuity, growth and reward of
value.

In personal life and macro-economics, productivity is usually a
measure of output based on input o2f0resources.
                                      THE WISDOM OF PRODUCTIVITY

Life success is primarily measured in terms of the output one generates
and not the capacity one possess. There are few things more frustrating
than having input but no output. Nothing more agonizing than to be
knowledgeable but broke, learned but failed, capacious but mediocre.
Productivity is the bridge between being full of potential and being full
of results.

Productivity is the ability to create, make and enhance product and
services that meet human and societal needs, it involves serving out the
products and services in excellence as well as creating a medium for
flow of returns to you. Productivity involves the ability to make
whatever you have or do more abundant and expansive. A productive
person always has profitable things to do.

When a person claims that there is no job or work, they are actually
claiming that there is no value they possess that can be productively
transacted for a return. When a person is fired from a job and can not
find something to do to generate finances, it either that the person has
developed extrinsic value more than intrinsic or that the person is
valuable but has not learned the art of being productive.

Be Productive with Your Value

It is possible to be valuable but not productive; it explains why one can
be a good cook, a great writer, a fantastic speaker but still broke and
jobless. Such one is valuable but not productive. Productivity is turning
one’s value and ideas to products and services and serving it to people
and thereby creating rewards. It is not merely valuable people that
become successful but productive people. Possessing value does not
guarantee wealth and rewards, being productive does. There are lots of
people that possess great value but are still poor and mediocre because

                                                              21
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

they camp at the realm of value. Productivity is actually the weapon for
success, wealth and economic victory. Financial resources flows
towards productive people, not necessarily valuable people.
Real productivity starts with a productive mindset. One of the reasons
for this book is to stimulate every reader to higher horizons of
productivity. Productive people are driven by multiplication and not
consumption therefore they master the art of delaying gratification.
Productivity-mentality are effective manager of their abilities, time and
resources.

More than ever, every person, family, church, ministry, business and
organisation must be determined to be productive. Failure is imminent
for the non-productive person or organisation. The only way to remain
productive is to be relentless in developing, deploying and adapting
your value to people’s current needs.

The Principle of Reward

The ultimate measure of productivity is profitability. No matter the
value one possesses or the efforts at its deployment, if one is not
making profit, one will soon be out. God loves profit. In fact, God says
in Isa 48:17, "I am the Lord your God, Who teaches you to profit, Who
leads you by the way you should go. Furthermore, Matt 25:30 says, ‘cast
the unprofitable servant into the outer darkness. There will be weeping
and gnashing of teeth.'

God is profit oriented and wants you to be. It should, however, be
noted that what describes profit to different persons and organisations
differ. For example, an individual should measure profit by the
fulfillment of personal purpose. A ministry or church should measure
profit by souls won, lives transformed, spiritual and physical growth of

                                                              22
                                      THE WISDOM OF PRODUCTIVITY

people reached and societal and national transformation. A business
measures profit by money made, needs met and corporate growth. This
means that when a church spends great money to win, perhaps, a few
souls, it has made profit. When a charity organisation spends a huge
amount of money to help a lot or a few people, it has made profit.

When a business spends a lot money and makes less than it spent, it
has made a loss. It is not all profit that is monetary. Fulfillment,
goodwill, joy and honour are intangible profit. However, there must be
profit- either tangible or intangible, accruing to you from the deploying
of your value. Don’t invest your life in an unprofitable venture. Profit is
the growth index in measure productivity, enterprise and success.

Value First and Profit Later

It is important to know that most times, when one starts out honing
skills and deploying value, one should not be profit driven but service
driven. Therefore it is always the initial phase of value deployment
when on makes the necessary sacrifices to selflessly serve out one’s
value even if it seems that no profit is accruing yet. This period is also
profitable as that is the time one is getting recognised for one’s value
and sowing seeds that will be harvested with time. So, it is good to be
profit oriented but one must not put profit before service. Your drive
should not be merely to make profit but to serve. However, a time
comes when profit becomes not just necessary but inevitable. Without
profit in the long run, there is no hope of expansion, continuity or
perpetuity of the value.

The concept of profitability and reward is key in value, productivity
and success. In actual sense there is nothing like a non-profit venture.
All venture must be for profit. The truth, however, is that not all profit
are

