based on the principle of reward. Are you making adequate profit or
being rewarded enough for what you do and represent? If you are doing
all to be done and still failing in life, it is either that you are doing the
wrong thing or doing the right thing the wrong way.

Reward Your Value

The principle of reward and profit is important especially in
productivity and enterprise. You need your value to be adequately
rewarded materially or intangibly so that you will have more input to
reinvest into growth, expansion and perpetuation of the value. When a
value is unrewarded, it will die out eventually to loss of the owner of
the value and the unrewarding users. Consumers of value who are not
willing to reward it are usually the first to move on to go and look
elsewhere when the dispensing of the value dries out due to lack of
adequate rewards to sustain and increase the source of the value. The
concept of rewards is very important in value, productivity and
enterprise because anything that is unrewarded will diminish and die
out. Rewards are not just the benefit of productivity, they are the
perpetrators and enhancers of it.

In candid words, one of the greatest injustice you probably have been
doing to your value, is that you have been under-pricing, underselling
or have been giving it free for too long. This might be a reason you do
not have resources to re-invest into developing it and also build a good
life of success for your self. Value only multiplies when it is rewarded.
If there is no reward, which could be material or intangible, value is
eventually frustrated into demise. This is the reason, God is an ardent
believer in rewarding people for value and inputs. According to Heb
11:6, He who comes to God must believe that He is, and that He is a
rewarder of those who diligently seek Him.

