What to Do with Value:

What do you have? A gift, an ability, an endowment, an expertise, a
positive character trait, a moral strength, a spiritual grace, a training
proficiency or certification, a handiwork or a talent? There must be
something you have. Productivity, enterprise and profitability with that
value you possess is the way to success.

The following are what to do with your value:

Discover it

No value is too little to be neglected. What you can do is a seed for
your success. Talking, writing, driving, teaching, cleaning, listening,
cooking . . . The list is endless. What is called self-discovery in the
school of success is actually the discovery of the value you possess. Do
not see what you do as small or irrelevant. View your value in a global
light.

Develop it

Many times, value in its raw form does not command the level of
reward or success one desires. So, it has to be refined and developed.
Education, training, studying, mentoring are tools for value
development. Work diligently till you become the very best in what you
do. Commitment to relentless personal development is the only ticket
to world class.

Deploy it

You must serve your value out to others. The more you add value to
others, the more your value increases. Deployment of value is key to its
multiplicity, growth and success. You will be shocked how big that
small can become when you start taking steps. It is advisable to create
or join a platform where you can dispense your value to people.

