                                 CHAPTER 4

   THE UNLIMITED WISDOM OF CHARACTER

In the school of leadership, greatness and success, the greatest asset
one can have is a strong character. Therefore, in attaining and
sustaining success, a wise area of personal investment is character
development. Character is having a strong personality, moral rectitude
and life disposition that is consistent with the highest values. Character
is the value, virtue and fortitude to be non-compromising in the face of
wrong alternatives and the ability to consistently live by highest
standards even when they are not convenient.

Knowledge, understanding and application of principles are often
emphasized in success, and rightly so. Truly, there are the right things
to do to attain success. However, life success is eventually at the mercy
of the strength of character of the person in question and not merely by
the principles practiced, because nothing delivers to people beyond
their character. This explains why different people seemingly do the
same things and get different results. Doing everything right but being
the wrong person will lead to a wrong outcome. In success, who you
are is more important than what you do. Your true character is
described by who you are when nobody is observing or monitoring
you. Since greatness and success is essentially an overflow of one’s
every day personality, practices and routines; a person’s character is
the greatest determinant of his or her level of success.

                                                              28
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

Can You Stand Success?

Your character determines what you will stand for and ultimately, what
you will fall for. As often said, the person who stands for nothing will
fall for anything. Most often, the truth about life is that it is equally, if
not more, demanding to sustain success than to attain it. Absolutely, it
is the character developed during the strenuous upward climb to
success that sustains one when one reaches the top. Many times, the
greatest gift life gives are the challenging processes on one’s way
towards greatness. This is because it is the traits, personality and
character developed in conquering those processes and challenges that
actually makes one become fit to sustain success. Most people who get
to a level of success without passing through the due process of
overcoming challenges on the way do not have the wisdom, strength
and character to manage the demands that accompanies that level of
success. Handing out success to a person as a mere act of benevolence
without allowing the person to develop the requisite strength of
character by walking the arduous road by themselves is
counterproductive; it produces people who are not able to sustainably
deliver at that level. This is the reason most people that win sums of
money in lottery soon lose it all through unwise spending while people
who built their wealth through nit and grit may lose all in an accidence
or misfortune and still build it all back from scratch. Real wealth is not
material and physical cash in possession but the wisdom, character and
personality developed during the process of wealth building. Character
is wealth.

Character Development - Digging Deep Foundations

Character is the foundation for success. In building engineering, the
foundation carries the entire load of the structure. Foundation are sub-
structures underneath the building and are mostly invisible but they are
built with great attention and strong materials as the strength of the
foundation determines the fate of th29e entire building.
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

Faults in foundation may not be obvious to the observer as they are
mostly hidden under the earth. However, a good builder will not
compromise a fault in the foundation for anything. When there is a
fault in the foundation of a building, no matter how hidden, it is only a
matter of time for this fault to amplify and bring the entire building
down. The taller a building rises, the more amplified the effect of a
fault in the foundation is. Similarly, the more successful a person
becomes, the more magnified flaws in the character becomes.
Character flaw will eventually catch up and bring down success, no
matter how long it takes.

The Scriptures aptly describes the fact that any admirable fruit seen on
a tree is only made possible because they are unseen roots that have
grown deep into the soil beneath the surface when it says, Once more a
remnant of the house of Judah will take root below and bear fruit
above. Success can be seen as a fruit with character as the root or as a
house with character as its foundation, metaphorically speaking.

Additionally, in the sport of weight lifting, athletes are not judged only
by the weight they can lift but also by how long they can stably stand
under that weight. It is very possible for one to lift a load but be unable
to stand under it. It is also dangerous to lift a load one can not stand
under because the weight may cause one to come crashing down and
incur injuries due to the crushing effect of the pressure of the load.
Strong character is the required stamina to stand under the weight of
success. It is dangerous to succeed to a level that one has not
developed the moral strength to stand stably at.

Reputation – The Stem of Character

One of the most important components of one’s success and greatness
is one’s reputation. Your reputation is how people think about you and
it is shown mostly by what people s3a0y about you especially behind you.
                              THE UNLIMITED WISDOM OF CHARACTER

It is the emotions and perceptions that come up whenever your name is
mentioned. In business, family, corporate leadership or as an
organisation, your reputation goes ahead of you and determines what
comes to you. Therefore, scripture says, it is important to choose a
good reputation over great riches; being held in high esteem is better
than silver or gold.

Reputation is an offshoot of character. The multi-billion industry of
advertising and branding is all about building a reputation. However, it
is known that great marketing of a substandard product is eventually
damaging. Without good content, advertising will only reveal the flaws
of the product to more people. The number one rule for advertising
and marketing is to make sure you are good at what you do and the
product will deliver on what it promises. Trying to build a reputation
without character is building a mansion with a pack of cards. It will
come crashing down. The best strategy to maintaining a great
reputation is to consistently maintain a strong character. Character
determines reputation. Reputation determines what comes to you
which determines your level of success. It is good to have it at the back
of your mind that everything you do and say contributes either to the
building or destroying your character?

Your reputation determines whether or not people will trust you or
work with you. One major thing people are looking for in all kinds of
relationship is trust. Even people who are not trust-worthy are looking
for someone they can trust? Therefore, everyone is looking for the
person of character.

As people seek a person of character to trust, so does God. When God

trusts you, He opens His treasures to you. God loves unconditionally

but He doesn’t trust unconditionally. He tests before He trusts. We

must see every challenge we face as a test of character before men and

God.  31
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

Additionally, every time we act or speak, we reveal our character to all.
A person without character has nothing no matter what he/she
possesses. People with great character may seem to have nothing
presently with time, however, their strength of character will produce
the material equivalent of their inward greatness.

Trials – The Test of Character

Life doesn’t trust you till it tests you. The challenges you face right now
are doing one thing – testing your character. A lot of people pray, plan,
work towards success but a good question is to ask yourself if you have
the character to sustain the level of success you are praying for. Any
man may achieve some material results through diverse means such as
compromise, skill or fraternities with the powers that be – physical and
spiritual powers. However, if you want success from God, God will not
give you what you cannot manage and what He is not sure you will still
stand for. Do you have the fortitude to be free and not be unrestrained?

Do you have the power to be high and not be proud? Do you have the
power to have control over people and systems and not be selfish? Do
you have the character to stand at the level of success that you have
been praying for? Wisdom said, ‘We can rejoice, too, when we run into
problems and trials, for we know that they help us develop endurance. And
endurance develops strength of character, and character strengthens our
confident hope of success’. The trials, challenges and problems you face
now are to strengthen you character by revealing areas of flaws and
shortcomings to be worked upon. When the test of character has been
passed, you are certified ready by life for the next level.

The Curse of Relativism

Character is the standard by which behaviour is measured. The
standard of good character compels one to do the right things when one
doesn’t feel like, when they are unpopular or sometimes, when they

                                                              32
                              THE UNLIMITED WISDOM OF CHARACTER

hurt. Self-imposition of high character standard is what makes a person
stand for right when nobody is there to check, monitor or supervise.
This lifestyle is only possible when there is an ideal that one holds to
and counts as superior to one’s desires, tendencies and results. In order
words, a person that will refuse to do wrong when it is the most
appealing, convenient and desirable thing to do is necessarily someone
who has something or someone higher than himself that he sets as an
ideal, holds himself accountable to and submits under the authority of.
Thus, believing and honouring God is the major compass and driver
for strong character and moral uprightness.

A person who believes in God accepts that there is one higher than he
is, whose pleasure he must win through compliance with standards and
whose displeasure as a result of breaking principles he must avoid.
Since God’s standard are high moral and character standards, faith and
honour for God became the pillars and guard posts for morality and
character since the inception of the human race. Removal of God from
our societal affairs was the demise of morality and good character.

Absolutism, as a philosophical concept, believes and maintains that
moral values are fixed regardless of time, place, and the people
concerned. Relativism believes that the concept of right or wrong are
not fixed but vary, depending on people, places, circumstances or
context. Relativism judges an action in terms of reasons and
explanations to determine whether it is wrong or right in that context.
Absolutism judges actions by an unbending rule of right and wrong and
demands people, places, circumstances and contexts to be tailored to
adhere to the absolute rule. The truth is that God is an absolutist and
His Word is the absolute.

One of the greatest injustice done to strong character in today’s world
has been the curse of relativism. Relativism makes people bend rules as
long as they get desired results. 33
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

People cheat to make progress, indulge in the most convenient
regardless of who suffers and satisfy self no matter who hurts. The sad
thing is that they are celebrated for doing this and used as the symbols
of success in the society. Relativism measures success by materialism
and measures right or wrong by whether the material goods were
delivered or not, the methods used is seen as inconsequential.

The decease of character was when human authorities began to bend
God’s absolutes and fit everything into man’s relativism. The end, they
say, justifies the means. Character dies out in a society when evil means
are used to achieve ‘good ends’. Furthermore, the ‘good ends’ are left
to individuals to relatively define. Then every body began to define
‘good end’ by ‘what is good for me’. Selfishness began to reign supreme
and character was dethroned.

A person of character will not adopt a wrong means even if it will
seemingly yield the desired end. For example, if the end justifies the
means, then one can falsify details to make money even if the system
would be damaged, opt out of a marriage to gain freedom even if the
kids would hurt or steal to get resources to meet one’s need even if the
owner of the resource would be disadvantaged. Strong character
demands that we stand resolute in the face of wrong alternatives and
stay on God’s absolute standard of character. A truly successful person
is one who has mastered self and stands absolutely for the standards of
character.

When these truths are said, critics are often quick to point out the
people that have no value for absolute standards and character and
have ‘succeeded’. They also point out how some people stick to God’s
absolutes and have ‘failed’. However, for such critics, a redefinition of
the concepts of success and failure is necessary. When we get the
correct definition of success, then we realize that a man without
character can never truly succeed. 34
                              THE UNLIMITED WISDOM OF CHARACTER

Success from a Higher Perspective

Life success is essentially fulfilling the utmost goal of one’s life, which
only the Creator of every life will determines A person could have
attained material relevance and still failed from an eternal perspective.
Real success can only be appraised when each person faces God, the
Maker and Judge to give account of life. At that point, it will be
obvious that material success while compromising on God’s standards
is not success.

Furthermore, even on earth, there are consequences faced when people
attain material results by violating the absolute standards of character.
Of course, it is quite true that some of those consequences may never
happen in the lifetime of those who caused them. However, legacy
always pays the nemesis for material success at the detriment of God’s
standards. The world today is facing the consequences of the past
‘successes’ of people who compromised the ethics of character.

Corruption, failed families, inadequate resources, global pollution,
suicide, recession and economic hardship, fraudulence and a lot more
problems today are because some people bent the rules some times
back to attain some seeming success. The truth about success is that it
can only be measured trans-generationally and eternally. Any success
attained that put future generations in jeopardy is failure. A person
who lived and acquired much but future generations later looked back
and cursed his memory actually failed. It is true that success without a
successor is failure and it is also true that success at the expense of
future generations is failure. A father is who acquired material success
but became the reason his children and future generations will bear an
evil name failed.

Therefore, we can only truly know whether you succeeded or not we
look at the world, your family, your35children and your legacy,
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

generations after you are gone. Also if we can peep into your eternal
