Succeed Intentionally

Success demands your pursuit while failure merely requires your
permission. In order words, success will not happen to you unless you
deliberately go after it while failure will happen to you even if you do
not pursue it. Therefore, one can fail by mistake but one cannot
succeed by mistake.

Have you ever given it a thought that every plant worthwhile needs to
be planted and cultivated while weeds grow easily on their own?
Similarly, a garden of flower only comes out perfect when carefully
tended and nurtured by someone. However, when left to itself, it
becomes overgrown with thorns and weeds. Hence, nothing left to
chance ever comes out well. You must live intentionally; do not leave
your life to chance. If you leave things to chance, they stand every
chance of going wrong.

Similarly, character development and building the right attributes and
attitudes for success will never happen by chance. You need to work
contentiously at it. It takes consistent discipline, regimented routines
and constant practices to develop great traits and a winning lifestyle.
While bad habits and poor practices that lead to mediocrity and failure
seem to come more naturally, the attitudes that make for success need
to be developed. Self-indulgence is the natural inclination of most
humans while self-mastery takes effort. Self-mastery is the seed for a
harvest of quality character. Character is one major seed for a harvest
of success.

                                                              36
                           THE UNLIMITED WISDOM OF CHARACTER

There are lots of laws that govern success – the fulfillment of your God-
given purpose in life. However, your character is a vital force. To be a
true success, you must not merely judge your character by your actions
but even your motives, thoughts and intentions. When you are really
ready for the high prize of successful fulfillment of life and purpose,
you will be more stringent on adhering to character standards by not
merely paying attention to your actions and your outward life but your
inner life as well. I know you have not changed figures and done the
deal that wrecked your financial reputation and credibility but what
about the tendency towards greed and dishonesty in your heart? If that
is still there, don’t celebrate yet, you need to work on it. You might not
have run off with another affair and failed your family, but the yet to be
outwardly expressed inner struggles with lusts and the weaknesses that
make you ‘want to’ are equally dangerous to you family success. In the
journey of success, you must be so meticulous that you pay attention
not just to actions but even tendencies. As you grow in knowledge,
principles, practices and understanding, also grow in character. You
shall succeed!

Some Success Character Traits

As we conclude on this chapter on the Unlimited Wisdom of Character
in Success, we want to identify some character traits and attributes that
need to be deliberately imbibed for maximal living. Note that these
may not come naturally to you, you need to work at them.

Honesty/Integrity: Integrity is the core character quality. It is a basic
measure of character. When you want to know a person of character,
give an integrity test. Integrity and honesty denote that a person’s word
is consistent with his/her action. Integrity transcends saying the truth,
it is living truthfully. If honesty is absent, there is a major character
flaw.

                                                         37
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

Discipline: Discipline is the ability to do what one ought to do even
when one does not feel like doing it. Discipline is a measure strength of
character. Indiscipline is self-sabotage; it is handing over the rudder of
one’s life-ship to convenience. If you allow the winds to drift a ship, it
will surely take it where the wind is headed and not necessarily where
the ship wants to go. Indiscipline takes you somewhere but never
where actually you wanted to go.

Hard-work/Diligence: Diligence is continual self-exertion in putting the
mental and physical effort required to deliver an expected result.
Diligence comes with the willingness to do things the way they should
be done and the grit not to quit until the work is done. There is a subtle
relationship between integrity and diligence. A good test of integrity is
to check a person’s work output. People of integrity generally pay the
price of hard-work to meet the expected standard. The one without
integrity probably has a plan to cover up and/or cut corners, so such a
person lazily does a substandard work. There is also a direct
relationship between diligence and discipline. Disciplined people
continue in diligence even when they feel like quitting.

Accountability: This is the willingness to be examined and held
answerable for one’s actions. Accountable people have a sense of being
responsible to a higher authority; human or divine, so they act with
self-imposed restraint. Lawlessness is an offspring of lack of
accountability. Externally imposed accountability is not a good
measure of a sense of responsibility. When you see a person who is
free, independent and yet accountable, you have met a one qualified for
success.

Chastity/Fidelity: No matter the relativist culture in today’s world,
sexual chastity and fidelity still remains a core character parameter.
Loose and multiple practices of sex is an advantage for baser animals
whose major purpose for copulation is recreation and procreation.
However, humanity is saddled with38the responsibility of family, duties
                              THE UNLIMITED WISDOM OF CHARACTER

of parenthood, the demands of marital trust, the complexities of
emotional management, preservation of individual ethics, propagation
of communal values, perpetuation of a responsible environment for
future generations and the pursuit of spirituality. Thus, loose sexual
practices are destructive to the character of humanity. Premarital, non-
marital, out-of-wedlock sex, same-sex marriages and multiple sexual
relationships all carry implications that necessarily will be eventually
harmful to human perpetuation and society. This statement is not
demean or profile any particular set of people. God loves all categories
of people and as His children, we should love all. However, everyone
must understand that the consequences of these practices will be
destructive to personal and societal framework in the long-run. So, it is
important to correct wrong acts because God frowns at the act though
He loves the people.

Boldness/Courage: Boldness and courage are admirable virtues. The
ability to take giant steps and dare great things are a display of strength
of character. Boldness makes heroes out of every day people.
Proactiveness, enterprise and the ability to take action is a character
trait that must be intentionally cultivated for anyone to become
anything worthwhile. Fear and timidity should be deemed as great a
flaw in character as immorality and dishonesty.

Dedication/Loyalty: Loyalty is a character trait whose import is best
seen when its opposite is demonstrated. We do not celebrate the virtue
of loyalty in people so much but we detest the display of disloyalty.
From simple betrayals to treason, lack of dedication to a course and
people reveals a major character deficiency. If you are in with a course
or a person, please be wholly in and stay in. Do not say you are in
when your heart is out.

Humility: Humility is one of the strongest character traits. It is
noteworthy that humility is not self3-a9 basement but an intentional
                                               WISDOM FOR LIVING

ondescension to do the lowly and menial as long as God is glorified.
Humility is necessarily accompanied by a healthy sense of self-esteem
and self-confidence born out of accurate self-perception. A humble
person is not struggling with a sense of inadequacy or inferiority
complex. Humble people know who they are and are secure in
themselves but still decide to reach down and do the needful no matter
how lowly it is. It takes humility to start small and grow big. The proud
person does not have the character to start small. Pride will prevent
success and even if it attains it, it will eventually self-destroy it.

Patience: This is another very important character trait. Patience is the
ability to wait for what you are working at to yield. It is a sense of
delayed gratification applied to everything one does in life. Patient
people are very powerful because they have the fortitude to stay at a
task long enough to achieve success out of it. A person can be diligent
but impatient. When diligence and patience meet, success is inevitable
no matter how long the walk.

Excellence: Excellence is the highest level of performance. Excellence is
applying the maximum sense of order to everything one does.
Excellence is the minimum requirement for outstanding performance
and success in today’s world. Excellence, as a character trait, shows in
everything one does: dressing, speech, work, home and environment.
Excellence is an attitude.

Prudence: Wisdom, discretion and prudence in decision making is
another character trait that is priceless. This is something that needs to
be worked out and developed continually as long as one lives. Nobody
can reach the end of wisdom, we all need to keep growing in wisdom,
judgement, discernment and prudence.

Love, Charity and Benevolence: Love is one of the most misunderstood
words in the world. Love is not an e40motion; it is a decision.
                              THE UNLIMITED WISDOM OF CHARACTER

Love is selflessness, sacrifice and putting the best interest of the loved
in consideration at all times, even ahead of one’s. Love is the highest
character value.
The list of character traits to develop for success is inexhaustible.
Others include optimism, respect, compassion/empathy, punctuality
etc. The truth is that when all is said and done, it is one’s character that
will eventually determine whether one will succeed or fail.

