                       ABOUT THE BOOK

There are essential resources for actualising one's purpose and
potential in life. Wisdom is principal among these essentials.
Wisdom entails knowing the 'What', 'When', 'How', 'Where' and
'With Whom' of every action in life. Thus, Wisdom for Living is
knowing the right thing(s) to do, the right time to do it, the right
place/environment, the right approach/method, as well as the
right relationships/associations to do it with in order to have a
fulfilled life.

This book is a sequel to The Life Assignment which explains the
'What of Life’ and The Times and Seasons of Life which examines
the 'When of Life'. Wisdom for Living shows the 'How, Where and
With Whom', thereby giving further insights into living a life of
fulfillment and meaning.

                             ABOUT THE AUTHOR

                                Davids Oluwaseye Ayodele is a trainer, speaker
                                and writer. He is graced with understanding
                                and presenting complex issues with simplicity
                                and clarity for practical application.

He is the founder of several initiatives both within the church and the
workplace, such as The Wisdom Institute of Leadership and Ministry for
training and equipping church leaders, ENABLED Multiconcept for
business and professional leadership development and consultancy, as
well as several other platforms for Bible-based teaching ministry. He has
a bachelor’s degree in chemical engineering and master’s degree in
engineering management from Ahmadu Bello University, Nigeria. He is
married to Deborah OluwaNifemi and they are blessed with children.

